# 🌿 Ghibli Community

A web application built for Studio Ghibli fans to discover movies, connect with other fans, and share their passion for the magical worlds created by Studio Ghibli.

The platform serves as a community hub where users can explore movies, discuss their favorite stories and characters, write reviews, and interact with other members who share the same interests.

---

## ✨ Features

- 🎬 Browse Studio Ghibli movies
- 📖 View detailed information about each movie
- ⭐ Rate and review movies
- 💬 Join discussions with the community
- 👤 User authentication and profiles
- ❤️ Save favorite movies
- 🔍 Search movies by title

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

### Frontend
- React
- Vite
- Tailwind CSS

### Backend
- Node.js
- Express.js

### Database
- MongoDB

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
GHIBLI/
│
├── frontend/    # React application
├── backend/     # Express API
└── README.md
```

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/sanalayouni/Ghibli.git
cd Ghibli
```

### Install Frontend

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
```

### Install Backend

```bash
cd backend
npm install
```

### Run the Frontend

```bash
npm run dev
```

### Run the Backend

```bash
npm start
```

---

## 📄 Environment Variables

Both the frontend and backend require environment variables.

Copy the example files and create your own `.env` files.

Frontend:

```
frontend/.env
```

Backend:

```
backend/.env
```

